<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enki</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enki was the Sumerian god of fresh water, crafts, wisdom and magic, known to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadians</a> as Ea. His chief temple, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/e-abzu">E-abzu</a>, stood at Eridu in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, which was regarded as his city. In myths he appears as a creator and helper of humanity, and in Enki and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ninhursag">Ninhursag</a> he provides the land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilmun">Dilmun</a> with fresh water.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enki.jpg" alt="Enki" width="265" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Enki(Ea).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
